# Consignment "Google Lens" email-button routing — LOCKED

This behavior is **required and permanent**. It was shipped in commit `a55f202`
("Default Outlook/mobile Google Lens button to the Bing bridge (fix empty search)")
and must NOT be regressed by any future change. The user explicitly asked that this
never be "switched up" again. If a change would alter any of the guarantees below,
STOP and confirm with the user first — do not "fix" it back to a simpler/direct flow.

## Required behavior (do not change)

1. **Email button links the SHORT token URL only.**
   The consignment email "Google Lens this item" button must point at
   `/api/consignment-lens/:token` (a short, query-string-free URL on this server).
   It must **never** embed the raw `https://lens.google.com/uploadbyurl?url=...`
   (~2 KB) link in the email. Outlook mobile SafeLinks ("Checking the link…")
   mangles long query strings, which produces an empty Google search.

2. **Outlook / mobile clients => 200 BRIDGE page (Bing first).**
   `GET /api/consignment-lens/:token` from a mobile UA or any Outlook client
   (including the Outlook-iOS in-app webview) must return a **200 HTML bridge page**
   that leads with **Bing visual search** (`bing.com/images/search`) plus an
   "Open Google Lens in Safari" option. It must **NOT** issue a `302` redirect
   straight to `lens.google.com/uploadbyurl`.

3. **Desktop browsers => 302 direct to Google Lens.**
   A desktop UA must get a `302` redirect whose `Location` starts with
   `https://lens.google.com/uploadbyurl?url=`. The fragile long Lens URL lives only
   in this server's `Location` header, never in the email.

4. **Overrides must keep working.**
   - `?lens=1` forces the direct Lens `302` even on a mobile/Outlook UA.
   - `?bridge=1` forces the Bing/Safari bridge page even on desktop.

## Why (so nobody "fixes" it back)

Google Lens `uploadbyurl` does **not** render inside Outlook's in-app webview — it
opens as a bare, EMPTY `google.com` search (confirmed by the user's screenshots).
The Bing visual search bridge is the **known-working** path inside the Outlook app
and on mobile. Sending Outlook/mobile straight to `lens.google.com/uploadbyurl` is
the exact bug that was fixed. Desktop Chrome/etc. handle `uploadbyurl` fine, so
desktop stays on the direct redirect.

## Hard rules for future agents

- **Do NOT** send Outlook or mobile clients straight to `lens.google.com/uploadbyurl`.
- **Always** keep the Bing bridge as the default for mobile/Outlook.
- **Keep** desktop on the direct Lens redirect.
- **Do NOT** put the long `uploadbyurl` link back into the email HTML — email links
  the short `/api/consignment-lens/:token` URL only.
- **Do NOT** weaken, rename-away, or delete the UA detection
  (`isMobile`/`isOutlook`) or the `?lens` / `?bridge` overrides.
- The regression tests in `tests/consignmentLens.test.js` lock this. If you change
  routing, the tests must still pass unchanged (don't relax them to make a
  regression go green). Run: `node --test tests/consignmentLens.test.js`.

## Where this lives

- Routing + UA branching: `routes/consignmentSubmission.js`
  (`GET /api/consignment-lens/:token`, `isMobile` / `isOutlook` / `wantBridge`).
- URL builders: `lib/consignmentPhotoHost.js`
  (`buildGoogleLensUrlForImage`, `buildBingVisualSearchUrlForImage`, `buildSafariHttpsUrl`).
- Email button wiring: `lib/consignmentEmail.js` (links the short token URL).
- Regression tests: `tests/consignmentLens.test.js`.
